Plymouth theme "arch-mono": black screen, the Arch logo draws itself as a glowing line,
a minimal passphrase field (dots, red shake on a wrong passphrase), and after unlocking
the logo fills with liquid as the boot progresses; full logo gets a bloom.

Build + install after editing gen.py (look) or arch-mono.script.in (behaviour):
  python3 gen.py out
  sudo rm -rf /usr/share/plymouth/themes/arch-mono
  sudo install -d /usr/share/plymouth/themes/arch-mono
  sudo install -m 644 out/* /usr/share/plymouth/themes/arch-mono/
  sudo plymouth-set-default-theme arch-mono
  sudo mkinitcpio -P            # the theme lives inside the UKI initramfs

Switch back to the Undertale one: sudo plymouth-set-default-theme sans && sudo mkinitcpio -P

Test build: python3 gen.py out --test appends test-timeline.script (fakes a wrong and a
right passphrase and the progress) and shows a frame counter. Every sprite in the script
must stay referenced by a variable or Plymouth frees it. Logo comes from
/usr/share/pixmaps/archlinux-logo.svg (package filesystem).
